{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1077313-mongolia-and-the-supernatural","id":1077313,"title":"Mongolia and the Supernatural","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-12T16:06:50-07:00","id":1077313,"title":"Mongolia and the Supernatural","content":"I've rooted around and tried to dig up info on this. I'm trying to figure out which tribe or tribes roamed the plains of Mongolia? What supernaturals go bump in the night? How far goes the beast court reach? I figure with how remote the area is not many mage orders have reached the area, possibly just Dreamspeakers for now. Technocracy? Doubt it other then occasional members from the asian branch entering the sea of grass to deal with threats. <br /> <br /> Info and ideas would be appreciated, I was debating making asian tribe that would native and unique to the area similar to the Uktena.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T16:08:56-07:00","id":1077317,"title":"","content":"Well there is that Legend about giant death worms","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T16:22:02-07:00","id":1077320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1077313-mongolia-and-the-supernatural?p=1077317#post1077317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well there is that Legend about giant death worms</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah the Mongolian Death Worms are a thing and the tunnels they bore are also noticed. Large cave tunnels with perfect smoothness with a faint acidic smell. This is a place Bygones might be able to manifest, Mongolia has not changed in form of faith since its early days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T16:30:01-07:00","id":1077328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freederp92</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1077313-mongolia-and-the-supernatural?p=1077320#post1077320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mongolia has not changed in form of faith since its early days.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually not entirely true. The spread of Buddhism in the 16th century had a significant impact on Mongolian culture and religious practice that persists to this day. Seven decades of communism have also shaped Mongolian cultural and spiritual life in profound ways that it is in many respects only recently emerging from, and it will be some time before the extent of its influence can really be assessed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T16:33:45-07:00","id":1077330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1077313-mongolia-and-the-supernatural?p=1077328#post1077328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's actually not entirely true. The spread of Buddhism in the 16th century had a significant impact on Mongolian culture and religious practice that persists to this day. Seven decades of communism have also shaped Mongolian cultural and spiritual life in profound ways that it is in many respects only recently emerging from, and it will be some time before the extent of its influence can really be assessed.</div> </div> </div> </div>True I forgot to account of the spread of Buddhism and the reign of communism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T16:43:34-07:00","id":1077335,"title":"","content":"If you're looking for some crazy historical shit with occult influences to mine for a Mongolian supernatural setting, this is the guy you are looking for.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_von_Ungern-Sternberg\" target=\"_blank\">The Bloody White Baron</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T18:20:02-07:00","id":1077381,"title":"","content":"Werewolf-wise, the Silent Striders, Uktena, Red Talons, Stargazers, and maybe Shadow Lords would be the most prevalent, IIRC. With the Fera, I think native fauna limit them to mostly Kitsune, Ratkin, and Corax. <br /> <br /> With Mages, the two biggest influences are going to be traditional Tengrism and Tibetan Buddhism, so you've got Dreamspeakers, the Akashic Brotherhood and to a lesser extent Ahl i Batan and Celestial Chorus. Also, the small shamanist society known as the Sons of Tengri.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T18:22:21-07:00","id":1077384,"title":"","content":"I personally place the Shadow Lords as the dominant tribe on the steppes there. I would also place some Stargazers on the local mountains. Possible Silver Fangs from the House of Blood Rest Crest. Bone Gnawers could also be present as rats live on the steppes (and they likely have plague reservoirs there).<br /> <br /> The other tribes would likely be completely absent, or perhaps a few visitors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T19:01:57-07:00","id":1077405,"title":"","content":"I would probably go with Stargazers, Silver Fangs, Silent Striders, and Wendigo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T19:02:42-07:00","id":1077406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1077313-mongolia-and-the-supernatural?p=1077381#post1077381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf-wise, the Silent Striders, Uktena, Red Talons, Stargazers, and maybe Shadow Lords would be the most prevalent, IIRC. With the Fera, I think native fauna limit them to mostly Kitsune, Ratkin, and Corax.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wind From the East also had Khan and Middle Dragons present. Shadow Lords Revised mentioned that there was a major division of the tribe there. Stargazers, if we believe the low numbers that they're supposed to have, will be among the least common of Garou there, or anywhere for that matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With Mages, the two biggest influences are going to be traditional Tengrism and Tibetan Buddhism, so you've got Dreamspeakers, the Akashic Brotherhood and to a lesser extent Ahl i Batan and Celestial Chorus. Also, the small shamanist society known as the Sons of Tengri. </div> </div> </div>They'd probably be more with the Disparates than the Traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T11:23:13-07:00","id":1077814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1077313-mongolia-and-the-supernatural?p=1077406#post1077406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wind From the East also had Khan and Middle Dragons present. Shadow Lords Revised mentioned that there was a major division of the tribe there. Stargazers, if we believe the low numbers that they're supposed to have, will be among the least common of Garou there, or anywhere for that matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly, the tiger no longer appears to exist in Mongolia, so there are probably no longer any native Khan outside the rare elder or younger homid-born member.<br /> (However, the snow leopard still lives in the region. I don't recall an official answer ever given about their prevalence among the Baghera, but in my own personal WoD, I've always seen them as the third, East Asian/Beast Courts branch of that tribe alongside the Indian/South Asian and African ones.)<br /> <br /> There do not appear to be any crocodilian species native to Mongolia, and dragons seem to have never played a huge role in the culture's mythology or imagery. So, Zhong Lung are likely to be transplants or homid-born, I suspect. A pity that, as I like the Zhong Lung. <br /> <br /> I've never really grokked the idea that the Stargazers are somehow supposed to be super rare (more so than the Red Talons). Their traditional stomping grounds exist at a geographic crossroads of Buddhism, Hinduism, Sufism, and Tengrism, which always offered up too many concepts and ideas for me to short sell them. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They'd probably be more with the Disparates than the Traditions. </div> </div> </div>I was listing mystic groups in general, not just Traditions. <br /> <br /> It occurs to me that there may be the odd (in more ways than one) Taftini in Mongolia. Tengrism is not all that incompatible with their mystical beliefs (that I'm aware of, at least).<br /> <br /> Also, psychics (or Orphan &quot;psychics&quot;) left over from Soviet era research experiments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T14:46:43-07:00","id":1077934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1077313-mongolia-and-the-supernatural?p=1077814#post1077814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sadly, the tiger no longer appears to exist in Mongolia, so there are probably no longer any native Khan outside the rare elder or younger homid-born member.<br /> (However, the snow leopard still lives in the region. I don't recall an official answer ever given about their prevalence among the Baghera, but in my own personal WoD, I've always seen them as the third, East Asian/Beast Courts branch of that tribe alongside the Indian/South Asian and African ones.)<br /> <br /> There do not appear to be any crocodilian species native to Mongolia, and dragons seem to have never played a huge role in the culture's mythology or imagery. So, Zhong Lung are likely to be transplants or homid-born, I suspect. A pity that, as I like the Zhong Lung.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it is a Vampire book, so there's also that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've never really grokked the idea that the Stargazers are somehow supposed to be super rare (more so than the Red Talons). Their traditional stomping grounds exist at a geographic crossroads of Buddhism, Hinduism, Sufism, and Tengrism, which always offered up too many concepts and ideas for me to short sell them. </div> </div> </div>Stargazers are supposed to be rare seer types and people Chimera tapped for what seems like primarily intellectual reasons. A number of other tribes pick up the slack at the same crossroads, which makes the continual painting of Stargazers as &quot;the Asian tribe&quot; that much more terrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T12:04:08-07:00","id":1080470,"title":"","content":"Are there any unique supernatural creatures to the region? Any Bygones that call the Steppes home? I can see the possibility of Wraiths hiding in dark places, the land was drenched in much blood over the years especially during the times of Genghis Khan and onward.<br /> <br /> I'm having a hard time find resources for myths of the sea of grass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T13:23:57-07:00","id":1080520,"title":"","content":"Iirc there are a vampire Clan named &quot;Anda&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1887-colognian","name":"Colognian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T13:48:43-07:00","id":1080534,"title":"","content":"Speaking of vampires in Mongolia:<br /> Among the Kindred we have Anda (a Gangrel bloodline), Gangrel (in general) and probably some Ravnos. Plus, some Wu Zao Salubri acting as shamans and holy men and wise women. It wouldn't surprise me if some <i>really</i> old Noiad are in torpor, there, too.<br /> Among the Kindred of the East, just about any Dharma might be found. I don't imagine Bone Shadows would be abundant, though they <i>would</i> be there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 04-18-2017, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T18:59:24-07:00","id":1080696,"title":"","content":"The Anda are dead. Killed by a ritual performed by the Giants of the East. Normal Gangrel may be present and possibly a few Ravnos. Maybe. The bulk of the clan fled the area long ago so it may be more along the line of a few brave individuals than any large number of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","name":"Chris Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T19:47:29-07:00","id":1080707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1077313-mongolia-and-the-supernatural?p=1080696#post1080696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Anda are dead. Killed by a ritual performed by the Giants of the East. Normal Gangrel may be present and possibly a few Ravnos. Maybe. The bulk of the clan fled the area long ago so it may be more along the line of a few brave individuals than any large number of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the Anda are dead. Canonically. The guy who started the thread can certainly have modern Anda, if he or she wants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T01:01:01-07:00","id":1080775,"title":"","content":"Two things lack of native beast breeds doesn't keep a fera group out of the area(or put it in the area or the game would be &quot;Kitsune, Ratkin and some dogs I guess&quot;) especially with the beast courts you have homids moving around some of their kin. Second it seems there's some level of truth in setting to hidden relic populations(Rage across the world 20 says there are wolves in Japan for example)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T06:55:35-07:00","id":1081421,"title":"","content":"A few tigers could wander in from Siberia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T01:06:14-07:00","id":1083887,"title":"","content":"I remember reading somewhere about there are some anda who in torpor and how they will awaken during the final nights I think it may have been in of the kindred of the east book I don't remember for sure so there's a possibility that the anda could one day return maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/962-the-viking-anarch","name":"the viking anarch","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T08:01:32-07:00","id":1083972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the viking anarch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1077313-mongolia-and-the-supernatural?p=1083887#post1083887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember reading somewhere about there are some anda who in torpor and how they will awaken during the final nights I think it may have been in of the kindred of the east book I don't remember for sure so there's a possibility that the anda could one day return maybe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in KotE proper, surely. It was a bit before Wind from the East was released, and there was no sign of the Anda to be found until the later book..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T15:11:59-07:00","id":1084176,"title":"","content":"Yes, the KJ had probably eradicated the last of the Anda five hundred years ago (I imagine that the KJ are very good at finding hidden Kindred because of their ability to use Spirits and Wraiths to find them). While the KJ may tolerate some pet Kindred like the Nagaraja, they would have especially despised the Anda after the Mongolian invasion of China and Korea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T15:35:56-07:00","id":1084189,"title":"","content":"'Pet' Kindred?<br /> <br /> The Kuei-jin are holding a viper to their throat, with both the della Passaglia Giovanni and the Nagaraja. Kuei-jin are basically super-Risen. Both the above-mentioned Kindred lineages are <i>necromancers</i>. The Kuei-jin are holding loaded guns to their own heads, while claiming the clips have no ammunition in them.<br /> <br /> And 'mastery of the spirit world' and 'using wraiths and spirits' to hunt down enemies? The Giovanni and the Nagaraja can both do that, too. <i>and</i> can ward against ghostly spies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 04-26-2017, 06:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T18:28:22-07:00","id":1084227,"title":"","content":"Never mind that Oliver Thrace, in Hong Kong---a Tremere elder!---has access to Ward vs Spirits (which, by the way, works on both spirits <i>and</i> ghosts), <i>and</i> possesses Dark Thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> EDIT: <i>And</i> invented Ward vs Cathayans, if I recall correctly.<br /> <br /> The Kindred are <i>not</i> 'easy prey' to Kuei-jin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 04-26-2017, 09:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T20:39:35-07:00","id":1084299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1077313-mongolia-and-the-supernatural?p=1084227#post1084227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never mind that Oliver Thrace, in Hong Kong---a Tremere elder!---has access to Ward vs Spirits (which, by the way, works on both spirits <i>and</i> ghosts), <i>and</i> possesses Dark Thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> EDIT: <i>And</i> invented Ward vs Cathayans, if I recall correctly.<br /> <br /> The Kindred are <i>not</i> 'easy prey' to Kuei-jin.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC Oliver Thrace sold out the Tremere chantry in Hong Kong when the changeover from British to Chinese rule happened and he's currently a &quot;guest&quot; of the Kue-Jin. Not saying they could destroy him easily, but there are a lot more of them than there are of him and even if he did want to escape/take over/whatever he'd lose the protection they offer him from the rest of the Tremere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T21:57:09-07:00","id":1084336,"title":"","content":"Other stuff?<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.sowhymongolia.com/6-iconic-mythical-creatures-mongolia/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.facebook.com/images/fb_icon_325x325.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.sowhymongolia.com/6-iconic-mythical-creatures-mongolia/\" target=\"_blank\"> Facebook - log in or sign up </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.sowhymongolia.com/6-iconic-mythical-creatures-mongolia/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.sowhymongolia.com/6-iconic-mythical-creatures-mongolia/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Log into Facebook to start sharing and connecting with your friends, family, and people you know. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T21:59:01-07:00","id":1084337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1077313-mongolia-and-the-supernatural?p=1084227#post1084227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never mind that Oliver Thrace, in Hong Kong---a Tremere elder!---has access to Ward vs Spirits (which, by the way, works on both spirits <i>and</i> ghosts), <i>and</i> possesses Dark Thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> EDIT: <i>And</i> invented Ward vs Cathayans, if I recall correctly.<br /> <br /> The Kindred are <i>not</i> 'easy prey' to Kuei-jin.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> He's an Akuma. That's sort of heavily cheating.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1077313-mongolia-and-the-supernatural?p=1084299#post1084299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC Oliver Thrace sold out the Tremere chantry in Hong Kong when the changeover from British to Chinese rule happened and he's currently a &quot;guest&quot; of the Kue-Jin. Not saying they could destroy him easily, but there are a lot more of them than there are of him and even if he did want to escape/take over/whatever he'd lose the protection they offer him from the rest of the Tremere.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You missed the parts where escaped and stole a bunch of sacred tomes, and turns out to be you know.. an Akuma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T22:39:52-07:00","id":1084347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1077313-mongolia-and-the-supernatural?p=1084337#post1084337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> You missed the parts where escaped and stole a bunch of sacred tomes, and turns out to be you know.. an Akuma.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, that is news to me. What book is that in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T23:03:47-07:00","id":1084353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1077313-mongolia-and-the-supernatural?p=1084347#post1084347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup, that is news to me. What book is that in?</div> </div> </div> </div>in HK:t his first write up has him as an infernalist with expertise on Eastern Demons. Its already implying he's Akuma then.<br /> There's a couple references to him in the various Dharma books which is basically goes from &quot;honored scholar who sells out the Cam&quot; to is given access to Boneflower secret libraries which he steals books from.<br /> <br /> He then is mentioned in SF as being the source of Ward vs KJ<br /> <br /> And Finally in the Time of Judgement the Yama Kings use him to usher in the sixth age by teaching the Tremere a ritual that kills all the KJ and causes much of Asia to merge with the Yomi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T08:06:06-07:00","id":1084486,"title":"","content":"....I mentioned he was a practitioner of Dark Thaumaturgy <i>in the very post I mentioned him first in</i>. So, yeah, he's an akuma. I acknowledged that, right out the gate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T08:28:28-07:00","id":1084496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1077313-mongolia-and-the-supernatural?p=1084353#post1084353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> in HK:t his first write up has him as an infernalist with expertise on Eastern Demons. Its already implying he's Akuma then.<br /> There's a couple references to him in the various Dharma books which is basically goes from &quot;honored scholar who sells out the Cam&quot; to is given access to Boneflower secret libraries which he steals books from.<br /> <br /> He then is mentioned in SF as being the source of Ward vs KJ<br /> <br /> And Finally in the Time of Judgement the Yama Kings use him to usher in the sixth age by teaching the Tremere a ritual that kills all the KJ and causes much of Asia to merge with the Yomi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha. Thanks for the rundown. I'll admit I'm a little unclear on what the difference is between an Akuma and a run-of-the-mill Infernalist besides locality, but I've also not really read much KJ material outside of the KotE corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T08:31:15-07:00","id":1084497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1077313-mongolia-and-the-supernatural?p=1084496#post1084496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gotcha. Thanks for the rundown. I'll admit I'm a little unclear on what the difference is between an Akuma and a run-of-the-mill Infernalist besides locality, but I've also not really read much KJ material outside of the KotE corebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Akuma specifically serve a Yama King and have some altered Traits to reflect things like not really dying unless their dark patron wants them to, not having to worry about frenzies in a manner similar to one of the DA Baali investiture options, and getting access to Soul Treatments to raise certain Traits to even more obscene levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T08:38:05-07:00","id":1084500,"title":"","content":"Akuma get short-term magical power in return for eternal damnation and eventually an eternity of torment for their shortsided stupidity.<br /> <br /> <i>Meanwhile...</i><br /> <br /> Infernalists get short-term magical power in return for eternal damnation and eventually an eternity of torment for their shortsighted stupidity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T16:34:55-07:00","id":1084756,"title":"","content":"As for Mongolian mages:<br /> Dreamspeakers and Verbena, to be sure. However, you might also find Euthanatos Buddhist monk-magi, Akashic Brothers and even Cult of Ecstacy shamans. Celestial Choristor missionaries could be easily imagined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}